Notes:
  * The VQE target includes the dyadic identity term; ansatz circuits do not need it.
  * Refine, coordinate, analytic, and analytic-direct modes all return parameters on the requested dyadic grid.
  * Coordinate mode tests axial +/-1 moves first, reducing the local 3^p factor to roughly 2p per round.
  * Analytic mode fits the exact low-degree one-coordinate trigonometric energy curves for this ansatz and jumps directly to target r.
  * Analytic mode has energy-query complexity approximately O(2^(p*r0) + B*p*L).
  * Analytic-direct removes the coarse search by using q_j=2^(r-3), the deterministic beta_j=pi/4 balanced seed.
  * For fixed harmonic degree its energy-query complexity is approximately O(p*L), independent of target precision r.
  * The balanced-start construction is polynomial; global convergence of the nonconvex VQE search is still heuristic.
  * All non-exhaustive search modes remain heuristic as global multi-parameter optimizers.
  * Use 'exhaustive' mode at feasible r to validate the refinement result.
  * G2 and G3 contain commuting Pauli terms, so n=0 has no Trotter error here.
  * This run is exact-statevector/noiseless; there is no shot noise yet.
